\pard\b\f0\fs24 Shai Siante\b0\f1\fs18\par
\b\f0\par
Ethnicity:\b0\f1  Argentinian.\par
\b\f0 Position:\b0\f1  Interpreter and Deep Space Medic Technician.\par
\b\f0 Age:\b0\f1  27.\par
\b\f0 Sex:\b0\f1  Female.\par
\b\f0 Height:\b0\f1  163 cm.\par
\b\f0 Build:\b0\f1  Small-framed and nimble.\par
\b\f0 Role in Story:\b0\f1  Squad medic, linguist and emotional stabiliser for John's team. She explains the Mark IV's life-support mesh and repeatedly keeps the team alive in the field.\par
\b\f0 Goal:\b0\f1  Master deep-space medicine, protect her team, and prove herself worthy of the responsibility John gives her.\par
\b\f0 Physical Description:\b0\f1  Slight, quick and precise in her movements. She often looks delicate beside the heavy armour, but once she starts working she becomes focused and assured.\par
\b\f0 Personality:\b0\f1  Gentle, curious, caring and quietly brave. Nervous in front of a room at first, but confident when speaking about medicine and patient care.\par
\b\f0 Occupation:\b0\f1  Deep Space Medic Technician with a linguistics background.\par
\b\f0 Habits/Mannerisms:\b0\f1  Speaks softly. Mothers patients and equipment alike. Prefers manual confirmation and hands-on procedure over blind faith in automation.\par
\b\f0 Background:\b0\f1  Worked pressure chambers and treated decompression illness on Ceres before her work ethic drew Marcellus's attention and she was reassigned into John's squad.\par
\b\f0 Internal Conflicts:\b0\f1  Uneasy about hidden vulnerabilities in the new suit systems, especially the possibility of cognitive compromise through autonomous tech.\par
\b\f0 External Conflicts:\b0\f1  Constantly placed in high-risk field conditions despite not coming from an engineering background.\par
\b\f0 Notes:\b0\f1  The neural buddy-system and DSK Mediguard suit her perfectly; she is one of the clearest examples of Serva Vitae technology being used to preserve life first.\par
